Absolutely. For a College Event Management System, you can design the ER diagram around events, students, organizers, venues, registrations, and participation.

Main Entities

1. Student
    * Student_ID (PK)
    * Name
    * Email
    * Phone
    * Department
    * Year
2. Event
    * Event_ID (PK)
    * Event_Name
    * Description
    * Date
    * Start_Time
    * End_Time
    * Event_Type
    * Status
3. Organizer
    * Organizer_ID (PK)
    * Name
    * Email
    * Phone
    * Department/Club
4. Venue
    * Venue_ID (PK)
    * Venue_Name
    * Location
    * Capacity
5. Registration
    * Registration_ID (PK)
    * Registration_Date
    * Status
    * Student_ID (FK)
    * Event_ID (FK)
6. Event_Category
    * Category_ID (PK)
    * Category_Name
    * Description
7. Club/Committee
    * Club_ID (PK)
    * Club_Name
    * Description
    * Contact_Email
8. Feedback
    * Feedback_ID (PK)
    * Rating
    * Comments
    * Feedback_Date
    * Student_ID (FK)
    * Event_ID (FK)
9. Event_Schedule (optional)
    * Schedule_ID (PK)
    * Activity_Name
    * Start_Time
    * End_Time
    * Event_ID (FK)